1090
00:48:32,280 --> 00:48:34,000
go to a family restaurant together.

1091
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:35,420
Sitting across from each other, across, across—

1092
00:48:35,420 --> 00:48:36,240
The conversation is weird too.

1093
00:48:37,240 --> 00:48:40,940
There are these awkward pauses in the conversation, it just stops for a moment.

1094
00:48:40,940 --> 00:48:42,680
Neither of us really wants to talk, especially—

1095
00:48:42,680 --> 00:48:45,700
W-wait, senpai, don't you have something you want to say?

1096
00:48:45,700 --> 00:48:49,240
N-n-n-no, I just... don't feel like talking right now.

1097
00:48:49,240 --> 00:48:57,060
Do you know how much courage it took for me to reach out to senpai and propose this collab?

1098
00:48:57,060 --> 00:48:59,240
I'm so grateful, really.

1099
00:48:59,240 --> 00:49:03,640
Well, apparently from the very beginning, Kiryu Coco-shi said she was fine with it, you know.

1100
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:05,380
I heard it from the manager.

1101
00:49:05,380 --> 00:49:07,380
Why though? Please tell me!

1102
00:49:07,380 --> 00:49:09,360
Well, because...

1103
00:49:09,360 --> 00:49:10,360
Dragon.

1104
00:49:10,360 --> 00:49:13,170
That's why.

1105
00:49:13,170 --> 00:49:14,010
Does everyone understand?

1106
00:49:14,010 --> 00:49:17,130
This socially awkward, awkward conversation—

1107
00:49:17,130 --> 00:49:20,890
This feeling of not quite being able to hold a conversation—

1108
00:49:20,890 --> 00:49:24,620
It's because she's a dragon.

1109
00:49:24,620 --> 00:49:26,180
It's like talking to a 2-year-old, isn't it?

1110
00:49:26,180 --> 00:49:26,740
No way!

1111
00:49:26,740 --> 00:49:27,440
Thank you very much.

1112
00:49:27,440 --> 00:49:28,280
No way!

1113
00:49:28,280 --> 00:49:29,260
She's a dragon.

1114
00:49:29,260 --> 00:49:30,700
It's because she's a dragon.

1115
00:49:30,700 --> 00:49:33,120
Oh, how old are you again, senpai?

1116
00:49:33,120 --> 00:49:34,420
3,501 years old.

1117
00:49:34,420 --> 00:49:34,520
*screaming*

1118
00:49:34,420 --> 00:49:36,420
Ahhh! It went up...

1119
00:50:02,820 --> 00:50:03,940
Huh?

1120
00:50:03,940 --> 00:50:05,320
It's advertising again.

1121
00:50:05,320 --> 00:50:07,660
That's weird.

1122
00:50:07,660 --> 00:50:10,700
Uh, so, yeah, got it.

1123
00:50:10,700 --> 00:50:14,640
Are we going to be okay from here on out?

1124
00:50:14,640 --> 00:50:16,080
We can't even hold a conversation anymore!

1125
00:50:16,080 --> 00:50:18,600
W-we can, we can! What's going on here?

1126
00:50:18,600 --> 00:50:21,060
We can, we can, we can!

1127
00:50:21,060 --> 00:50:24,840
I was trying to steer us into a smooth wrap-up!

1128
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:26,800
Even so, how are you as a hostess?

1129
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:29,000
If you're aiming to be the number one hostess queen,

1130
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:30,900
try having a smooth conversation!

1131
00:50:30,900 --> 00:50:32,460
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

1132
00:50:32,460 --> 00:50:34,700
Oh, again?

1133
00:50:34,700 --> 00:50:37,500
You came back? Coco-saaaan!

1134
00:50:37,500 --> 00:50:38,430
I came back again!

1135
00:50:38,430 --> 00:50:39,460
I came back again!

1136
00:50:39,460 --> 00:50:40,300
You're so cute, I just had to request you again!

1137
00:50:40,300 --> 00:50:42,700
Excuse me, may I sit next to you?

1138
00:50:42,700 --> 00:50:43,520
Oh, please, go ahead!

1139
00:50:43,520 --> 00:50:45,560
What would you like to drink today?

1140
00:50:45,560 --> 00:50:46,860
Oh, today...

1141
00:50:46,860 --> 00:50:49,060
I've already had a bit too much to drink,

1142
00:50:49,060 --> 00:50:51,160
so maybe just something light for the next two hours, please.

1143
00:50:51,160 --> 00:50:51,920
Something light?

1144
00:50:51,920 --> 00:50:54,740
Yeah, something sweet,

1145
00:50:54,740 --> 00:50:58,160
and something with a little fizz to it.

1146
00:50:58,160 --> 00:51:02,440
Nice, the way you just cozied right up like that.

1147
00:51:02,440 --> 00:51:05,440
Hey, you there in the black suit — bring us some sparkling wine!

1148
00:51:05,440 --> 00:51:09,440
Thank you so much, I appreciate it!

1149
00:51:09,440 --> 00:51:14,240
You're so cute — even a little tipsy, you're adorable today!

1150
00:51:14,240 --> 00:51:15,240
Let's toast, cheers!

1151
00:51:15,240 --> 00:51:16,840
Cheers, please!

1152
00:51:16,840 --> 00:51:20,640
Let's drink up!

1153
00:51:20,640 --> 00:51:25,640
As expected, you really are wonderful.

1154
00:51:25,640 --> 00:51:32,440
Dai-chan, every time I see you, those horns have such an amazing black shine to them!

1155
00:51:32,440 --> 00:51:36,320
These horns are gleaming — they're totally bling-bling!

1156
00:51:36,320 --> 00:51:38,400
Huh? Bling-bling?

1157
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:40,500
Bling-bling!

1158
00:51:40,500 --> 00:51:46,720
Just for you, I polished them up even more today — they're super shiny and sparkling!

1159
00:51:46,720 --> 00:51:48,050
Wow, amazing!

1160
00:51:48,050 --> 00:51:50,020
This is the super-shiny version?

1161
00:51:50,020 --> 00:51:51,880
They're totally dazzling!

1162
00:51:51,880 --> 00:51:54,840
Ready to go anytime!

1163
00:51:54,840 --> 00:51:55,620
Really?

1164
00:51:55,620 --> 00:51:59,700
Senpai, I don't know why, but...

1165
00:51:59,700 --> 00:52:02,580
there's a bomb here.

1166
00:52:02,580 --> 00:52:04,400
A bomb? At a hostess club?

1167
00:52:04,400 --> 00:52:06,820
Leave it to me, leave it to me!

1168
00:52:06,820 --> 00:52:09,060
There's a bomb at the hostess club!

1169
00:52:09,060 --> 00:52:10,400
It's a hostess club!

1170
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:13,760
Of course there's a bomb — when a cute girl like you is around,

1171
00:52:13,760 --> 00:52:15,360
bombs are bound to show up!

1172
00:52:15,360 --> 00:52:16,580
Senpai, I have the Dragon Radar!

1173
00:52:16,580 --> 00:52:17,460
This is the Dragon Radar!

1174
00:52:17,460 --> 00:52:19,100
I have the Dragon Radar!

1175
00:52:19,100 --> 00:52:26,620
4 from the top, 4 from the top, 5 to the right, 4 from the top — the 3rd from the right has a ○○.

1176
00:52:26,620 --> 00:52:30,300
4 from the top, and how many from the right?

1177
00:52:30,300 --> 00:52:32,900
3 from the right, Senpai!

1178
00:52:32,900 --> 00:52:36,020
4 from the top, 3rd from the right.

1179
00:52:36,020 --> 00:52:41,160
That location isn't in my manual at all.

1180
00:52:41,160 --> 00:52:43,020
Explain it to me again from the beginning.

1181
00:52:43,020 --> 00:52:48,420
Oh right. 4 from the top — wait, there are two, both 4 from the top.

1182
00:52:48,420 --> 00:52:50,240
Okay.

1183
00:52:50,240 --> 00:52:58,020
To the right — the far right, and then left, left.

1184
00:52:58,020 --> 00:53:02,080
Got it. What color are both of those lights?

1185
00:53:02,080 --> 00:53:04,000
Green.

1186
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:06,880
Both of them are green?

1187
00:53:06,880 --> 00:53:08,260
Yes, that's right.

1188
00:53:09,780 --> 00:53:11,760
Is there no white light?

1189
00:53:11,760 --> 00:53:12,760
The white light is...

1190
00:53:12,760 --> 00:53:14,560
upper right,

1191
00:53:14,560 --> 00:53:16,360
from the top,

1192
00:53:16,360 --> 00:53:18,360
second one,

1193
00:53:18,360 --> 00:53:20,160
far right.

1194
00:53:20,160 --> 00:53:23,160
Second from the top, far right?

1195
00:53:23,160 --> 00:53:25,960
What do you mean?

1196
00:53:25,960 --> 00:53:28,960
Second from the top, far right.

1197
00:53:28,960 --> 00:53:30,760
From the top,

1198
00:53:30,760 --> 00:53:32,760
second from the top, far right.

1199
00:53:32,760 --> 00:53:37,760
Second from the top, far right.

1200
00:53:37,760 --> 00:53:42,300
Move it down, down, down, down — all the way to the bottom.

1201
00:53:42,300 --> 00:53:42,960
We did it!

1202
00:53:42,960 --> 00:53:47,920
Ah, s-sorry, um, the triangle goal is, probably, um...

1203
00:53:47,920 --> 00:53:48,670
Where is it?

1204
00:53:48,670 --> 00:53:52,460
It's the third from the top in the leftmost column.

1205
00:53:52,460 --> 00:53:58,200
Third from the top in the leftmost column, right?

1206
00:53:58,200 --> 00:54:00,760
Got it. Go one to the left first.

1207
00:54:00,760 --> 00:54:02,300
One to the left?

1208
00:54:02,300 --> 00:54:04,320
Then go up two.

1209
00:54:04,320 --> 00:54:07,220
Ah, two up, sorry, driver! Two up!

1210
00:54:07,220 --> 00:54:09,620
Then go one more up.

1211
00:54:09,620 --> 00:54:11,120
Yes, one more up, senpai!

1212
00:54:11,120 --> 00:54:11,920
Okay, done!

1213
00:54:11,920 --> 00:54:13,120
Then go one to the left.

1214
00:54:13,120 --> 00:54:13,820
Okay, one to the left!

1215
00:54:13,820 --> 00:54:14,520
Oh, amazing!

1216
00:54:14,520 --> 00:54:17,020
Now go down, down, down all the way to the bottom!

1217
00:54:17,020 --> 00:54:18,620
Ahh, amazing, so amazing, amazing, amazing!

1218
00:54:18,620 --> 00:54:19,320
Oh, amazing, amazing!

1219
00:54:19,320 --> 00:54:21,720
Now slide all the way to the left, left, left, left to the far end!

1220
00:54:21,720 --> 00:54:23,620
Just keep going left!

1221
00:54:23,620 --> 00:54:26,120
I've pushed it right into the left corner!

1222
00:54:26,120 --> 00:54:27,820
Now just go straight up!

1223
00:54:27,820 --> 00:54:29,320
Just go straight up!

1224
00:54:29,320 --> 00:54:30,820
We did it! That's insane!

1225
00:54:30,820 --> 00:54:32,590
WHAAAAT?!

1226
00:54:32,590 --> 00:54:33,420
Perfect!

1227
00:54:33,420 --> 00:54:34,420
Ohh!

1228
00:54:34,420 --> 00:54:37,220
Senpai, want to do a rematch on the alphabet one?

1229
00:54:37,220 --> 00:54:39,020
Here we go again.

1230
00:54:39,020 --> 00:54:41,820
Five letters — want to try it?

1231
00:54:41,820 --> 00:54:43,620
Go ahead and say the letters.

1232
00:54:43,620 --> 00:54:52,020
X... and scrolling down: N... V... I... T... C...

1233
00:54:52,020 --> 00:54:56,620
X... N... O... V... I...

1234
00:54:56,620 --> 00:54:57,420
"Yes"

1235
00:54:57,420 --> 00:54:58,220
"Yes"

1236
00:54:58,220 --> 00:54:59,020
"T"

1237
00:54:59,020 --> 00:54:59,820
"S"

1238
00:54:59,820 --> 00:55:00,820
"S"

1239
00:55:00,820 --> 00:55:01,620
"E"

1240
00:55:01,620 --> 00:55:05,620
"What buttons are on that panel over there?"

1241
00:55:05,620 --> 00:55:08,220
"Seven-mi"

1242
00:55:08,220 --> 00:55:10,020
"Seven-mitch"

1243
00:55:10,020 --> 00:55:11,820
"Same-ba-ton, huh"

1244
00:55:11,820 --> 00:55:13,620
"Same-" "Got it"

1245
00:55:13,620 --> 00:55:16,620
"If you scroll through that button..."

1246
00:55:16,620 --> 00:55:20,620
"What letters can the leftmost alphabet character be set to?"

1247
00:55:20,620 --> 00:55:21,420
"Go ahead and say them."

1248
00:55:21,420 --> 00:55:28,060
"X" "M" "F" "E" "I" "T" "C"

1249
00:55:28,060 --> 00:55:29,840
No! The timer!

1250
00:55:29,840 --> 00:55:32,060
Help me, senpai!

1251
00:55:32,060 --> 00:55:33,120
Ahh, scary!

1252
00:55:33,120 --> 00:55:36,320
Right, right, okay then, I got it.

1253
00:55:36,320 --> 00:55:38,920
"N" "N" "T"

1254
00:55:38,920 --> 00:55:41,520
Is what's displayed now the word you just said?

1255
00:55:41,520 --> 00:55:43,360
No, it's the word I scrolled down to.

1256
00:55:43,360 --> 00:55:46,920
The word I scrolled down to.

1257
00:55:46,920 --> 00:55:48,780
The word you scrolled down to — say it again.

1258
00:55:48,780 --> 00:55:57,780
X? M? X! L! V! I! T! C! Y! Y is NO! Y! NO!

1259
00:55:57,780 --> 00:56:01,780
Then rearrange those letters to spell THESE.

1260
00:56:01,780 --> 00:56:07,180
T... H? T... H... E... S... E

1261
00:56:07,180 --> 00:56:15,190
E... S... no S! No S!

1262
00:56:15,190 --> 00:56:16,190
There's no S!

1263
00:56:16,190 --> 00:56:17,190
No S!

1264
00:56:17,190 --> 00:56:20,190
T-H-I-N-G! T-H-I-N-G!

1265
00:56:20,190 --> 00:56:23,790
T-H-E... no...

1266
00:56:23,790 --> 00:56:25,590
T-H-I-X...

1267
00:56:25,590 --> 00:56:29,590
I? Huh? T-H-E-I... huh? huh? huh? huh? huh?

1268
00:56:29,590 --> 00:56:31,590
Everyone, is T-H-I-N-G possible?

1269
00:56:31,590 --> 00:56:34,590
T-H-I... T-H-I... what comes after I?

1270
00:56:34,590 --> 00:56:35,390
Bing!

1271
00:56:35,390 --> 00:56:36,190
No I?

1272
00:56:36,190 --> 00:56:39,190
There's an I! There's an I! I is there! I is right there!

1273
00:56:39,190 --> 00:56:40,990
I... I-N-G!

1274
00:56:40,990 --> 00:56:47,510
Yes, yes, yes, NC, N, NO, no, NO, N, NO, N, NO, N it is, NO, N, NO, N

1275
00:56:47,510 --> 00:56:49,870
No N! Pike, pike!

1276
00:56:49,870 --> 00:56:52,150
Set it to B, H, R, E, E.

1277
00:56:52,150 --> 00:56:54,950
Set it to E? But I think I'm about to...

1278
00:56:54,950 --> 00:56:55,830
B, H, R

1279
00:56:55,830 --> 00:57:03,350
Huh? T, H, okay, still alive, still alive — but if it explodes here, Coco, Coco-senpai gets caught in it too!

1280
00:57:03,350 --> 00:57:05,610
T, H, E

1281
00:57:05,610 --> 00:57:07,610
D.H.E.?

1282
00:57:07,610 --> 00:57:09,610
D.H.E.R.E.E.3

1283
00:57:09,610 --> 00:57:11,610
3? 3? 3?

1284
00:57:11,610 --> 00:57:13,610
D.H.R.E.E.3

1285
00:57:13,610 --> 00:57:15,610
D.H.R.R.

1286
00:57:15,610 --> 00:57:20,320
And so, another junior's

1287
00:57:20,320 --> 00:57:22,320
life was lost.

1288
00:57:22,320 --> 00:57:24,120
Killer Coco

1289
00:57:24,120 --> 00:57:25,920
only came to hang out,

1290
00:57:25,920 --> 00:57:27,720
and yet she's killed her junior 5 times—

1291
00:57:27,720 --> 00:57:29,720
5 or 6 times, I've lost count—

1292
00:57:29,720 --> 00:57:31,720
it seems she's done it again.

1293
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:33,520
Everyone, thank you so much

1294
00:57:33,520 --> 00:57:36,580
for joining Polka's stream today.

1295
00:57:36,580 --> 00:57:37,680
Thank you very much.

1296
00:57:37,680 --> 00:57:40,560
This little fennec

1297
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:41,080
what was it again—

1298
00:57:41,080 --> 00:57:43,540
this damn little fennec,

1299
00:57:43,540 --> 00:57:45,420
this damn little fennec,

1300
00:57:45,420 --> 00:57:47,540
I don't think she'll ever come back to life,

1301
00:57:47,540 --> 00:57:49,260
wrap it up!

1302
00:57:49,260 --> 00:57:51,400
And so,

1303
00:57:51,400 --> 00:57:53,560
thank you so much for today!

1304
00:57:53,560 --> 00:57:54,360
Chairman Coco,

1305
00:57:54,360 --> 00:57:56,960
please continue to take care of me going forward!

1306
00:57:56,960 --> 00:57:59,960
Thank you very much!

1307
00:57:59,960 --> 00:58:02,480
And with that,

1308
00:58:02,480 --> 00:58:03,300
here we go—

1309
00:58:03,300 --> 00:58:06,160
heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho!

1310
00:58:06,160 --> 00:58:08,300
And Chairman Coco zooms off!

1311
00:58:08,300 --> 00:58:09,500
Oh, only the lightning bolt was left behind.

1312
00:58:09,500 --> 00:58:10,500
Zoom!

1313
00:58:10,500 --> 00:58:12,700
Went out with an explosion

1314
00:58:12,700 --> 00:58:13,700
after all.

1315
00:58:13,700 --> 00:58:15,200
Went out with an explosion?

1316
00:58:15,200 --> 00:58:16,300
Yeah, went out with an explosion!

1317
00:58:16,300 --> 00:58:17,000
Next time—

1318
00:58:17,000 --> 00:58:18,000
going out with an explosion is the best!

1319
00:58:18,000 --> 00:58:18,400
Next time—

1320
00:58:18,400 --> 00:58:18,800
Oh!

1321
00:58:18,800 --> 00:58:21,300
Shishiro Botan and Watame-senpai

1322
00:58:21,300 --> 00:58:23,100
are doing a collab!

1323
00:58:23,100 --> 00:58:24,400
Amazing!

1324
00:58:24,400 --> 00:58:25,900
Everyone go check it out!

1325
00:58:25,900 --> 00:58:27,180
Party!
